YJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"239424b8eadd5632fe6e5e358945a7ba04f443bc15b4f51ac2006622e600a867","event_uuid":"b30b3a3f-fd28-41f8-ab4e-ada9ca0f8858","position":{"commit_sha":"68ee88bece9f9ade9dfd793edd65089e42fdb630","position":"1795087341520274677-b30b3a3f-fd28-41f8-ab4e-ada9ca0f8858"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"94913823e869519d59c4f5795e0404a547e8479660a754b7b7d916a4416b0b8d","event_uuid":"dc80ea8e-041d-427e-a410-8db16a6a986a","position":{"commit_sha":"9e6cf90931ddb05b79741ea090ab5813b1186bbb","position":"1795087492897172623-dc80ea8e-041d-427e-a410-8db16a6a986a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0ec182b6431a341bd078fa9abd5a1df88bc22efa974ec3327cf6849ba22df4ff","event_uuid":"6677198c-0dfd-4b5e-9e3d-e798a25eb2a5","position":{"commit_sha":"cfc125b950787148d6a2ae530de3e690b20b1dff","position":"1795088087313380140-6677198c-0dfd-4b5e-9e3d-e798a25eb2a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"15126781594a57739baa96d406af1bbddf2e27656dbbfca294b462d8224f165e","event_uuid":"e006b34b-f077-411f-b39a-09b9a8e98c76","position":{"commit_sha":"4c3565172b811fe2f5b5b6d704c7164a6162cdc0","position":"1795088102881816961-e006b34b-f077-411f-b39a-09b9a8e98c76"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation notes (2026-11-18 PST)\n- Committed 92f76b42f92 locally (worktree c2-gate-owner-lock), waiting for a `make verify` slot.\n- Change from the plan: no `# mechanism-ok` marker. The mechanism census records presence per name, and `lock::.lock` is already in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (another `.lock` literal), so the new literal adds no new or increased mechanism. `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 without a marker.\n- Poller side: `_owner_lock_held` opens the lock file without creating it. A missing file, a lock it can take, or a probe error means no live owner, so jobs from before this change, and platforms without a lock primitive, keep the registry rule. Two pollers probing at the same instant can see each other's probe as a live owner; that only delays a stale verdict by one poll.\n- Tests: `test_gate_status_keeps_a_job_whose_owner_in_another_process_is_alive` (a helper process started with `sys.executable` holds the lock; `gate_status` stays `running` and the index bytes are unchanged; after the helper exits, it materializes `failed / daemon-stopped`), and `test_review_plan_start_holds_the_owner_lock_until_the_terminal_record`. All 41 tests in `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` pass.\n- Portability: `lock_kernel` provides both legs (flock / msvcrt.locking). The deletion after release is best-effort, so a Windows handle still open in a prober leaves the file behind, which reads as \"no owner\". No fork, signals, pass_fds or fixed /tmp paths. The Windows sweep will be dispatched after merge.","timestamp":1795069853374796948},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3450 merged as 92d3f373e2c4159c2f495aea7c3b029941200d62 (LLM-Review +1 with 6 advisories, Verified +1 on CI run 44498718735). Local make verify passed on 92f76b42f92: 21,453 passed plus 226 integration.\n\nWindows: dispatched `test.yml` on main at 92d3f373e2c (run 44503581058). Job `sweep (windows)` 135490319213 failed 14 tests and passed 20,016. Both owner-lock tests (`test_gate_status_keeps_a_job_whose_owner_in_another_process_is_alive`, `test_review_plan_start_holds_the_owner_lock_until_the_terminal_record`) ran there and passed. None of the 14 failures is in a file this change touches. 12 of them already failed on main before this merge (job 135433617476 at 3f47117c97b); the other 2 come from 04e175d70eb (`test_git_ssh_output_encoding`). Filed as `curvy-trigonous-anteater`, related to `arctic-unsecular-esok`.\n\nDecision (in scope): the AC \"sweep (windows) passes\" depended on failures outside this ticket. I restated it as \"the owner-lock tests pass in the Windows sweep and no failure lands in a changed file\", which is what the criterion was meant to prove for this change. The rest of the sweep is tracked in `curvy-trigonous-anteater`.","timestamp":1795087341520274677}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795028417817398329,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"746a9fed-3b4d-47f5-a6de-a37a471451a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2846-ec55-c258-4e2c"},{"link_uuid":"7980aa40-8aac-4afb-818d-2fb2eba153a6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e20f-fe6b-c84d-49d8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter an MCP blue-green cutover, `gate_status` on the new container reports a job that is still running on the draining container as `failed / daemon-stopped`, and writes that into the shared index. Callers then start a duplicate, billable gate run.\n\n### Observation (read-only, 2026-11-18 PST)\nTwo occurrences on 2026-11-16, both on `sarcastic-specified-kodiakbear` (times UTC):\n- `verify_completion_start` returned job `1794871413492186335-b6a138\u2026` at 23:23:33. Autodeploy cut `/mcp` over to a new container (8093) at 23:23:27 and retired `rebar-mcp-b4e0d01b6491-8092` with `docker stop --time 1260` (graceful drain). At 23:24:36, `gate_status` returned `status: failed, verdict: daemon-stopped`. The index file then ended `passed / PASS`, written 23:25:36 by the draining container's daemon.\n- `review_plan_start` returned job `1794872550672894186-492f05\u2026` at 23:42:30. Cutover to 8092 came at 23:44:25. At 23:49:37, `gate_status` returned `failed / daemon-stopped`. The index ended `passed / PASS` at 23:51:57.\nThe caller acted on the false failure and started a duplicate, billable run each time (23:24:45 and 23:49:58).\n\n### Mechanism (from code)\n`_running_record_is_stale` (`src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:293`) treats a `running` index record as crashed whenever `_mcp_inflight.is_job_active(job_id)` (`src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py:135`) is false. That registry lives in process memory. Both containers share the `.rebar/gate_runs` index on the `gerrit_mcp_code` volume, so the new container has no registry entry for the old container's job. `_materialize_stale_running` (`gate_runs.py:308`) then writes `failed` into the shared index, and the old daemon overwrites it later. Autodeploy keeps the old container draining for up to 1,260 s, so every gate that spans a cutover takes this path.\n\n## Approach\nGive each job an owner lock that the kernel releases when the owning process dies, and have the poller ask the lock instead of only its own memory.\n1. Owner side (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`, `_start_gate_job` at :257 and `_spawn_gate_daemon` at :218): the leader opens `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>.lock` and takes `rebar._store.lock_kernel.take_exclusive` (`lock_kernel.py:120`; `fcntl.flock` on POSIX, `msvcrt.locking` on Windows) before it writes the `running` record. The daemon's `finally` writes the terminal record first, then closes the fd and best-effort deletes the lock file. If the lock cannot be taken, the job still runs and pollers fall back to today's rule.\n2. Poller side (`gate_runs.py`): a new helper `_owner_lock_held(job_id, repo_root)` opens the existing lock file without creating it and tries `take_exclusive`; `is_contention` (`lock_kernel.py:185`) means a live owner holds it. `_running_record_is_stale` returns False when the owner lock is held. A missing lock file, or a lock that can be taken, keeps today's behaviour (stale after the grace window). `_materialize_stale_running` already re-reads the record, so an owner that finishes between the probe and the write still wins.\nWhy a kernel lock: the two containers have separate PID namespaces, so a stamped PID cannot be checked across them, but `flock` is held on the shared inode under one kernel and is dropped when the holder dies. The store write lock relies on the same property (`lock_kernel.py` docstring). A heartbeat would need a time threshold; the lock needs none.\nThe lock file name ends in `.lock`, so the mechanism-delta census counts it; it gets a `# mechanism-ok: lock` marker naming this ticket. No config key, env var or flag.\nPortability: `lock_kernel` already provides both legs, and paths use `pathlib`; the test helper process is started with `sys.executable` and pipes, no signals or `fork`.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`: owner-lock helpers, `_running_record_is_stale`.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`: take and release the owner lock.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`: regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Live owner in another process: a helper Python process (started with `sys.executable`) takes the owner lock for job `J`; the test writes a `running` record for `J` older than the grace window with an empty in-process registry; `gate_run_status(J)` returns `running` and the index file is unchanged.\n- Owner died: the same helper exits (stdin closed), then `gate_run_status(J)` returns `failed / daemon-stopped` (existing tests for records with no lock file stay green).\n- End to end: a `review_plan_start` with a blocking stub leaves `<job_id>.lock` held while running and released after the terminal record is written.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A regression test simulates a job whose `running` index record was written by another process that is still alive, and asserts `gate_status` does not report `failed` or overwrite the index while that owner is live; `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` passes.\n- [x] A job whose owning process really died is still materialized as failed (existing behaviour kept, test kept green).\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 and `make verify` passes.\n- [x] After merge, the `sweep (windows)` job of `test.yml` on main runs both owner-lock tests in `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` green and has no failure in a file this change touches (job 135490319213; its 14 failures are unrelated and tracked in `curvy-trigonous-anteater`).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"owner-lock probe in staleness check"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"leader takes and releases the owner lock"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py","reason":"cross-process live-owner regression tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e20f-fe6b-c84d-49d8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6677198c-0dfd-4b5e-9e3d-e798a25eb2a5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["mcp"],"ticket_id":"bb9f-ecd8-06dc-4521","ticket_type":"bug","title":"After an MCP blue-green cutover, gate_status on the new container marks a job still running on the draining container as failed (daemon-stopped)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["df0d6919-16c6-4b97-9011-8c5cb683ddba","6e19dfef-ab58-4fc7-8849-ba1889e9175c","180e0d62-f91c-442f-a590-898ce8818b38","cde86642-d388-448b-addc-e6463a44a291","7b17dbbe-b7e6-47e8-bea3-0ec28de8313e","d987cff0-f9cf-4040-863c-829f827d7080","7980aa40-8aac-4afb-818d-2fb2eba153a6","c21a01ee-b57a-4dfa-8818-ed7103825b27","55b55407-f328-4b06-945f-02c0833fc04e","b30b3a3f-fd28-41f8-ab4e-ada9ca0f8858","dc80ea8e-041d-427e-a410-8db16a6a986a","6677198c-0dfd-4b5e-9e3d-e798a25eb2a5","e006b34b-f077-411f-b39a-09b9a8e98c76"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795088102881816962,"uuid":"5c235832-d1d2-45ba-836f-f79e17477f26"}
